{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "id": "x32-compact-cc",
  "name": "Behringer X32 Compact (DAW Remote, MIDI CC)",
  "notes": "Behringer X32 Compact used as a control surface via its DAW Remote mode with protocol 'MIDI CC' (SETUP > Remote > MIDI CC, interface Card MIDI = X-USB, Remote engaged). HARDWARE-VERIFIED 2026-07-26 by live MIDI capture against a real unit: the left fader bank sends CC 0-7 on channel 1, the right (bus) bank CC 72-79, the main fader CC 70 - all absolute 0-127, and all motorized: the console moves the fader when it receives the same CC back. The MUTE row is the only host-controllable button row in this mode: buttons send CC on channel 2 with the strip's fader number (127 pressed / 0 released) and their LEDs follow received channel-2 CCs (verified blinking). Select/Solo rows, the encoders and the master section do NOT transmit in CC remote mode - deliberately not declared. The console occasionally broadcasts state groups (e.g. CC 40-43 / 60-63 / 80-85 on channel 2) when layers change; these are ignored because no declared control matches them. Note the Mackie Control remote protocol never engaged on this unit during testing (kept sending raw CC), which is why this definition targets CC mode.",
  "manufacturer": "Behringer",
  "mode": "standard",
  "defaultMidiChannel": 1,
